…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEYe see how large a letter I have written unto you with mine own hand.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›As many as desire to make a fair shew in the flesh, they constrain you to be circumcised; only lest they should suffer persecution for the cross of Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„For neither they themselves who are circumcised keep the law; but desire to have you circumcised, that they may glory in your flesh.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut God forbid that I should glory, save in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, by whom the world is crucified unto me, and I unto the world.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdFor in Christ Jesus neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book/§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd as many as walk according to this rule, peace be on them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYFrom henceforth let no man trouble me: for I bear in my body the marks of the Lord Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙGBrethren, the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.¦layout ‚¤textÙ%Unto the Galatians written from Rome.¦layout¥blankªlast_verse